fit log(spread) = a + b*log(S) over S = 3, 5, 9, 17, 33; solve spread = 1
b near -0.5 is the sqrt-N law and the extrapolation is credible; b near 0 means
the spread does not shrink with seeds at all and NO seed count fixes the verdict.

